###############################################
## Dynamic implicit analysis: HHT method (idx_eqa=2, alpha=-0.1)
## Bar of twenty 361 elements with the lateral DOFs fixed, so that it carries
## an axial wave. Step 1 applies a tip step load and step 2 doubles it.
## Each jump excites the high-frequency modes (w*dt up to 2), which the HHT
## method damps while it keeps the fundamental mode (w*dt = 0.079).
## The initial tip velocity with the mass-proportional damping gives a nonzero
## initial acceleration, which the force history of the HHT method starts from.
## gamma and beta are not used since the HHT method derives them from alpha.
## Restart run: Step 2 only (reads restart from step 1 end, which has to
## carry the force history of the HHT method)
###############################################
!VERSION
 3
!SOLUTION, TYPE=DYNAMIC
!DYNAMIC
 2, 1
 0.0, 40.0, 40, 1.0
 0.5, 0.25, -0.1
 1, 1, 0.01, 0.0
 100, MONITOR, 100
 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1
!RESTART, FREQUENCY=-20
!VELOCITY, TYPE=INITIAL
 TIP, 3, 3, 0.1
!BOUNDARY, GRPID=1
 FIX, 3, 3, 0.0
 LATERAL, 1, 2, 0.0
!CLOAD, GRPID=2
 TIP, 3, 0.5
!SOLVER,METHOD=CG,PRECOND=1,ITERLOG=NO,TIMELOG=NO
 500000, 2
 1.00e-10, 1.00, 0.0
!STEP, SUBSTEPS=20
 1.0, 20.0
 BOUNDARY, 1
 LOAD, 2
!WRITE,RESULT,FREQUENCY=10
!OUTPUT_RES
 DISP,ON
 VEL,ON
 ACC,ON
!END
